Unit: SDD

Purpose:
  Unit testing — verify individual components in isolation. Unit tests
  are the foundation of the test pyramid: fast, cheap, and provide
  immediate feedback.

Owns: ./

Scope:
  Single function, method, class, or component
  Isolated from external dependencies
  No database, network, or file system access (unless mocked)

Principles:
  One assertion per test (preferred)
  Test behavior, not implementation
  Fast execution (< 1s per test)
  Deterministic (no flaky tests)
  Independent (no test order dependency)

Structure:
  Every unit test MUST:
    test a single unit of behavior
    be independent of other tests
    clean up after itself
    fail with a clear message

  Unit test naming:
    <Function>_<Condition>_<ExpectedResult>
    e.g. Refund_AlreadyExists_ReturnsExistingRefund

Frameworks:
  Go: testing, testify, gomock
  Laravel: PHPUnit, Mockery
  Node: Jest, Vitest, Sinon
  React: Jest, React Testing Library
  Vue: Vitest, Vue Test Utils
  Angular: Jasmine, TestBed

Coverage:
  Minimum coverage: project-defined (typically 80%)
  Critical path coverage: 100%
  AI MUST NOT use coverage as the sole quality metric

Navigation:
